# Skip to my Lou - Amerikaans volkslied en dansspel
# Traditioneel Amerikaans lied uit de jaren 1840, een dansspel waarbij van partner
# gewisseld wordt (Wikipedia (en), "Skip to My Lou"). Publiek domein.
# Overgenomen uit SKIPTOMY.LOU (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). Tikfouten hersteld: "nuttermilk" werd
# "buttermilk", "skip my Lou" werd "skip to my Lou". De bron zet het refrein
# vooraan en zegt niet waar het terugkomt; daarom geen herhalingen toegevoegd.
{title: Skip to my Lou}
{meta: id skip-to-my-lou}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit SKIPTOMY.LOU (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); herkomst via Wikipedia (en), Skip to My Lou}
{meta: tag kampvuur}
{meta: tag volkslied}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_chorus}
She's gone [Eb]again, skip to my Lou
She's gone [Bb7]again, skip to my Lou
She's gone [Eb]again, skip to my Lou
[Bb7]Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[Eb]Flies in the buttermilk, two by two
[Bb7]Flies in the buttermilk, two by two
[Eb]Flies in the buttermilk, two by two
[Bb7]Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
All to the center, skip to my Lou (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Ladies to the center, skip to my Lou (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Gents to the center, skip to my Lou (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Promenade all, skip to my Lou (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Swing your partner, skip to my Lou (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
To your opposite, skip to my Lou (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
If you can't get a red-bird, a blue bird'll do (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
I've lost my girl, now what'll I do (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
I'll get another, a better one too (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Pa's got a shotgun, number 32 (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Hurry up slowpoke, do, oh, do (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
My girl wears a number nine shoe (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
When I go courting, I take two (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Gone again, now what'll I do (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
I'll get another one sweeter than you (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
He's got big feet and awkward, too (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Kitten in the haymow, mew, mew, mew (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
I'll get her back in spite of you (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
We'll keep it up 'til half past two (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
One old boot and a run-down shoe (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Stole my partner, skip to my Lou (3x)
Skip to my Lou, my darling.
{end_of_verse}
